Subject: [PATCH] pvrsgx 1.6: gate SGX lockup watchdog on outstanding work

SGXOSTimer declares a hardware lockup whenever the EDM task counter is unchanged
for three samples while the SGX is powered; its only exemption is powered-down.
A powered-but-idle SGX (parked EDM counter, empty kernel CCB, no BIF traffic)
therefore false-trips HWRecoveryResetSGX. Patch 0009 raised the active-power
latency to 500 ms, keeping the SGX powered through inter-frame and teardown idle
gaps and making these false recoveries common (HWRecovery storms with
BIF_FAULT=0, kernel CCB WO==RO, BIF_MEM_REQ_STAT=0).

Gate the lockup counter on actual outstanding work: only treat a parked EDM
counter as a lockup when the kernel CCB is not drained or a BIF memory request
is in flight. A genuine hang keeps work outstanding, so real lockups are still
detected; an idle SGX no longer resets. Decouples lockup detection from the APM
latency and keeps 0009's power-lock fix intact.

Not upstream behaviour: SGXOSTimer is unchanged through DDK 1.14 (only a
per-workload OpenCL grace counter was ever added, and SGX530 has no OpenCL).
---
 .../pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c   | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
index 3d2fd1dd6..356935bca 100755
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/pvrsgx/1.6.16.3977/services4/srvkm/devices/sgx/sgxinit.c
@@ -1169,0 +1170 @@ IMG_VOID SGXOSTimer(IMG_VOID *pvData)
+	IMG_BOOL		bIdle = IMG_FALSE;
@@ -1179,0 +1181,7 @@ IMG_VOID SGXOSTimer(IMG_VOID *pvData)
+	/* Busy-gate: a parked EDM counter on an idle SGX (kernel CCB drained and no
+	   outstanding BIF memory requests) is not a lockup; a real hang keeps work in
+	   flight, so genuine lockups are still detected. */
+	bIdle = (!bPoweredDown)
+		&& (psDevInfo->psKernelCCBCtl->ui32ReadOffset == psDevInfo->psKernelCCBCtl->ui32WriteOffset)
+		&& (OSReadHWReg(psDevInfo->pvRegsBaseKM, EUR_CR_BIF_MEM_REQ_STAT) == 0);
+
@@ -1182 +1190 @@ IMG_VOID SGXOSTimer(IMG_VOID *pvData)
-	if (bPoweredDown)
+	if (bPoweredDown || bIdle)
